B.Zh=new A.acD("Rules and Regulations for the Use of Facilities and Amenities","To ensure the proper, safe, and responsible use of campus facilities and amenities, all Campus Users and External Clients are required to observe the following rules and regulations:\n\n## 1. Reservation and Authorization\n1. Facilities and amenities may only be used with a confirmed and authorized reservation through the CSU-A SmartReserve system.\n2. Users must provide accurate and complete information when making a reservation.\n3. Users must only use the facility on the approved date and within the approved reservation time.\n4. Unauthorized use of a facility or extension beyond the approved reservation period is not permitted.\n5. Any request to extend the reservation must be coordinated with and approved by the office in charge.\n\n## 2. Extended Use and Additional Charges\n1. Users must strictly observe their approved reservation schedule.\n2. Campus Users whose activities extend beyond 5:00 PM shall be responsible for any applicable charges or payment required for the extended use of the facility, subject to the policies of the office in charge.\n3. External Clients who extend their use beyond their approved reservation period shall be charged an additional fee based on the applicable facility and amenity rates and the additional duration of use.\n4. Users must obtain approval from the office in charge before extending their activity or use of the facility.\n5. Users must not assume that continued use beyond the approved time is automatically permitted.\n6. The office in charge may require users to vacate the facility if an extension is not authorized or if the facility is reserved for another user.\n7. All applicable additional charges must be settled according to the payment procedures of the office in charge.\n\n## 3. Payment and Charges\n1. External Clients must settle the applicable facility and amenity charges before their reservation is confirmed.\n2. Additional charges may apply to External Clients who extend their reservation beyond the approved time.\n3. Campus Users may be subject to applicable charges when their activities extend beyond 5:00 PM.\n4. Users are responsible for any applicable charges resulting from extended use, additional amenities, damages, or other authorized services.\n\n## 4. Proper Use of Facilities and Amenities\n1. Facilities and amenities shall only be used for the purpose stated in the reservation.\n2. Users must take proper care of all facilities, equipment, furniture, and amenities.\n3. Users must not move, alter, damage, or remove any facility property without permission from the office in charge.\n4. Any damage, loss, or misuse of campus property must be reported immediately to the office in charge.\n5. Users must maintain cleanliness and order within the facility before, during, and after use.\n\n## 5. Safety and Proper Conduct\n1. Users must observe all applicable campus safety, security, and emergency procedures.\n2. Activities that may endanger people, damage property, or disrupt campus operations are not permitted.\n3. Smoking, vandalism, and other prohibited activities are not allowed in designated facilities.\n4. Users must maintain proper and respectful behavior while using the facilities.\n5. The office in charge may stop any activity that violates facility rules or poses a safety or security concern.\n\n## 6. Proper Use of Amenities\n1. Amenities included in a reservation shall only be used during the approved reservation period and for their intended purpose.\n2. Users must report any existing damage or malfunction of amenities to the office in charge immediately.\n3. Users must not use or request additional amenities without proper authorization.\n4. Lost, damaged, or improperly used amenities may be subject to replacement costs or corresponding charges.\n\n## 7. Monitoring and Compliance\n1. All facilities and amenities are monitored and managed by the office in charge.\n2. The office in charge may verify reservations, monitor facility use, inspect facilities and amenities, and ensure compliance with these rules and regulations.\n3. Users must cooperate with authorized personnel during inspections, verification, and monitoring activities.\n4. Incidents involving unauthorized use, extended use, misuse, damage, or violations may be documented by the office in charge.\n5. Failure to comply with these rules may result in additional charges, cancellation of the reservation, suspension of facility-use privileges, or other appropriate administrative action.\n\n## 8. End of Reservation\n1. Users must vacate the facility promptly at the end of the approved reservation period unless an extension has been properly authorized.\n2. Facilities and amenities must be returned in a clean and orderly condition.\n3. Users must remove all personal belongings and materials after use.\n4. Any damage, incident, or concern discovered after use must be reported immediately to the office in charge.\n\n## 9. Acknowledgment\nBy making and using a reservation through CSU-A SmartReserve, users acknowledge that they have read, understood, and agreed to comply with these rules and regulations, as well as other applicable policies of Cagayan State University\u2013Aparri Campus.\nThe office in charge reserves the right to monitor the use of facilities and amenities and implement appropriate measures to ensure their proper, safe, and responsible use.\n",1,"rules")
B.Zi=new A.acD("CSU-A SmartReserve Terms and Conditions","Welcome to **CSU-A SmartReserve**, an AI-enhanced facility reservation system of Cagayan State University\u2013Aparri Campus. By creating an account or logging in and using the system for the first time, you agree to comply with the following Terms and Conditions.\n\n## 1. Account Responsibility\n1. Users must provide accurate and complete information when creating or using an account.\n2. Users are responsible for keeping their account credentials confidential and must not share their account with another person.\n3. Users must immediately report any suspected unauthorized access or misuse of their account to the appropriate administrator.\n4. Accounts may be suspended or restricted for violations of these Terms and Conditions or applicable campus policies.\n\n## 2. Reservation\n1. Users must provide accurate information when submitting a facility reservation.\n2. A reservation is considered valid only after it has been properly processed and confirmed through CSU-A SmartReserve.\n3. Users may only use the facility on the approved date and within the approved reservation period.\n4. Users must not make reservations for unauthorized activities or purposes that violate campus rules and regulations.\n5. Users are responsible for cancelling or modifying their reservation when necessary and must follow the applicable reservation procedures.\n\n## 3. Payment and Extended Use\n1. **Campus Users** who extend their activities beyond **5:00 PM** shall be responsible for any applicable charges or payment required for the extended use, subject to the policies of the office in charge.\n2. **External Clients** are responsible for the applicable facility and amenity charges associated with their reservation.\n3. External Clients who extend their use beyond the approved reservation period shall be charged additional fees based on the applicable rates and duration of the extension.\n4. Any extension of facility use must be approved by the office in charge.\n5. Users are responsible for settling applicable charges before or after extended use, according to the payment procedures established by the office in charge.\n\n## 4. Facility and Amenity Use\n1. Users agree to use facilities, equipment, and amenities responsibly and only for their intended purposes.\n2. Users must maintain cleanliness and proper order within the facility.\n3. Users must not damage, alter, remove, or misuse any campus property.\n4. Any damage, loss, or malfunction must be reported immediately to the office in charge.\n5. Users may be held responsible for applicable costs resulting from damage, loss, or improper use.\n\n## 5. Monitoring of Facilities and Amenities\n1. **All facilities and amenities are monitored and managed by the office in charge.**\n2. The office in charge may verify reservations, monitor facility use, inspect facilities and amenities, and document incidents related to their use.\n3. Users agree to cooperate with authorized personnel during verification, inspection, and monitoring activities.\n4. Unauthorized use, misuse, damage, or violation of facility rules may result in appropriate administrative action.\n\n## 6. Compliance with Rules\n1. Users agree to comply with the CSU-A SmartReserve Rules and Regulations for the Use of Facilities and Amenities.\n2. Users must also comply with applicable policies, regulations, and guidelines of Cagayan State University\u2013Aparri Campus.\n3. Failure to comply may result in cancellation of reservations, additional charges, suspension of facility-use privileges, account suspension, or other appropriate action by the office in charge.\n\n## 7. System and Information\n1. CSU-A SmartReserve is intended to facilitate facility reservations, reservation management, payments, notifications, and related services.\n2. Users are responsible for reviewing the information they submit before confirming a transaction or reservation.\n3. System-generated information, including reservation status, charges, notifications, and recommendations, should be reviewed by the user and may be subject to verification by the office in charge.\n\n## 8. Agreement\nBy selecting **\u201cI Agree\u201d**, creating an account, or continuing to use CSU-A SmartReserve, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to these Terms and Conditions and the applicable Rules and Regulations for the Use of Facilities and Amenities.\nIf you do not agree to these Terms and Conditions, please do not proceed with account creation or use of the system.\nFor concerns regarding reservations, payments, facilities, amenities, or account access, please contact the appropriate office in charge.\n",0,"terms")
